[h1]Raze Forever[/h1]

Archaon is not the only one who can end the world. Next to the usual [b]Raze[/b] option, every culture now gets [b]Raze Forever[/b]: the settlement is wiped off the map and its ruins can never be occupied or colonised again — by anyone, you included.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Raze Forever[/b] after capturing a settlement, for every culture except Nagash's Undead Legions (devastation is already their thing).
[*]The ruins get the devastated look and a permanent occupation block — the same engine mechanism Archaon uses on his Lord of the End Times path, not an "AI won't go there" trick.
[*]Erase more than half of a province and the land itself burns — only for those who fit the lore:
[list]
[*]Chaos wasteland: Warriors of Chaos, Khorne, Nurgle, Slaanesh, Tzeentch, Daemons, Beastmen, Norsca, Chaos Dwarfs
[*]Skaven blight: Skaven
[*]Nagash's dead land: Vampire Counts, Vampire Coast
[*]Everyone else leaves the land as it is — no Bretonnian Chaos wastelands.
[/list]
[*]No corruption, no climate change, no bonuses. Same cost and loot as that culture's normal Raze, minus faction raze rewards (skulls, chivalry, souls…), which stay with the vanilla option.
[*]Human players only: the AI never gets a permanent block from it.
[*]Plays nice with Archaon's Destroyer path: his own script still devastates the province and counts it for his bonuses and long victory.
[/list]

[h2]Languages[/h2]
Works in every game language out of the box: the option reads [b]"Raze: Scorched Earth"[/b] and the ruins say [b]"Cannot Colonise"[/b], built from the game's own translations.
Optional translation patches (separate items) add the full texts with a detailed tooltip: English, Russian, German, French, Italian, Spanish, Polish, Czech, Turkish, Brazilian Portuguese, Korean, Simplified and Traditional Chinese.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Safe to add to a running campaign.
[*][b]Do not remove it mid-campaign[/b] — saves may fail to load and erased ruins could become settleable again.
[*]Adds new rows only, overwrites no vanilla tables. Factions added by other mods do not get the option.
[/list]

[h2]Known behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]On the very first tutorial capture of some campaigns ("Attack the enemy" mission) the game ignores any raze, vanilla included. Later captures work normally.
[*]When an endgame crisis ends, the game may clear devastation visuals in its area; the ruins stay blocked.
[/list]
